From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 02:20:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebPlayer: let inputstreamhelper install a web app's Widevine
 CDM

Web apps such as Netflix need the Widevine CDM that inputstream.adaptive
keeps in its decrypter path, but nothing installs it for them: Python
add-ons call inputstreamhelper's check themselves, and web apps run no
code in Kodi. Before it opens a web app that imports
script.module.inputstreamhelper while pages have no CDM, the web player
runs the helper's check_inputstream for Widevine behind a busy dialog,
which steps back for the helper's own dialogs. The app opens whatever
the user decides.

The client reads the CDM directory once when it starts, so a client
that started with another CDM than the one installed now, whoever
installed it, is restarted before the next web app opens. A view
requested while the client restarts is asked for when the client is up
again.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
